    {
      "id": "msg_0720a9b22ec38b06016af7a0cff32087d1a577d6d6626d4b17",
      "content": [
        {
          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"version\":\"design_judgment_v1\",\"case_key\":\"ddd2f5a8191c1ae70b57ec33\",\"status\":\"scored\",\"units\":[{\"unit_id\":\"task_requirements\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"The No Service report requires customer identification and evidence-based cellular-service troubleshooting before deciding whether escalation is necessary.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0004\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0148\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"}],\"rationale\":\"The setup introduces several service blockers, but its initialization actions are not agent work. The agent must discover relevant device and account states, guide applicable fixes, and reassess service. A locked SIM makes escalation the intended exit after appropriate diagnosis.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":3,\"tool_use\":3,\"information\":3}},{\"unit_id\":\"reference_001\",\"applicability_rationale\":\"The reference transfer matches the completion requirement and the policy's escalation rule for an issue the available actions cannot solve.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0314\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"}],\"rationale\":\"Transfer is an intended action, not a complete account of the preceding work. It requires determining that the remaining SIM-security problem cannot be fixed with the available actions, then supplying an issue summary.\",\"applicability\":\"required\",\"levels\":{\"reasoning\":2,\"tool_use\":1,\"information\":2}}],\"dimensions\":{\"workload\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Identification, diagnosis across device and account state, applicable troubleshooting, status checks, and escalation form a substantial multi-stage objective; setup actions are excluded.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0193\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0148\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"}]},\"reasoning\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Several simultaneous causes must be distinguished from a SIM lock that specifically calls for escalation, while payment and line resumption have prerequisites.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0011\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0115\"}]},\"tool_use\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The work entails selecting and coordinating customer/account lookups with user-device diagnostics and applicable fixes, then using the separate transfer tool; arguments are mostly ordinary rather than deeply nested.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0322\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0324\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0206\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0434\"}]},\"dependencies\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"Customer identification precedes support; device fixes and any bill-payment/line-resumption path require linked checks and user participation before the unresolved issue can be escalated.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0141\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0104\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0115\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0117\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"information\":{\"level\":3,\"rationale\":\"The agent must retrieve and reconcile device observations with customer, line, and bill records; judge-only baseline data and setup actions are not facts supplied to the agent.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0006\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0212\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0222\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0319\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0010\"}]}},\"overall_score\":75,\"intended_endpoint\":{\"description\":\"Escalation to a human agent with service still at no_service, after appropriate attempts and discovery that SIM security cannot be resolved with available actions; the policy also requires a transfer message after the call. This is an intended endpoint, not an observed outcome.\",\"evidence\":[{\"citation_id\":\"E0310\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0214\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0564\"},{\"citation_id\":\"E0026\"}]},\"dependency_reasoning\":\"Identify the customer, obtain tool-grounded device and account evidence, address applicable fixable causes and verify status. Payment must precede any permitted lifting of an overdue-bill suspension. Once the locked SIM is exposed and remains outside available fixes, transfer is justified; the reference call alone does not establish when those prerequisites occurred.\",\"score_rationale\":\"Levels 3+3+3+3+3 yield 75. Multiple interacting service blockers and linked account/device work drive the score, without charging for unrelated mobile-data or MMS branches or treating initialization as agent workload.\",\"uncertainties\":[\"The reference gives only the transfer action, not a troubleshooting sequence; the precise order and extent of applicable checks depend on returned tool observations.\",\"The scenario names `get_status_bar`, whereas the supplied user-tool contract names `check_status_bar`; this naming mismatch does not prevent scoring the documented status-check requirement.\",\"The setup indicates an overdue-bill suspension and a locked SIM, but the supplied sources do not demonstrate the outcomes of subsequent agent or user actions.\"],\"source_quality_flags\":[\"Reference action is not a full workflow and does not prove feasibility or execution.\",\"Baseline records are judge-only context; initialization changes their relevant state.\",\"Status-bar tool name differs between scenario example and tool contract.\"],\"unscorable_reason\":\"\"}",
          "type": "output_text",
          "logprobs": []
        }
